{"title":"Ocean of Stars: A Painted Poem About How to Bear the Astonishment of Life","link":"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/10/02/ocean-of-stars-azita-ardakani/","date":1790996709000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"446\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_cover.jpg?fit=320%2C446&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"Ocean of Stars: A Painted Poem About How to Bear the Astonishment of Life\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_cover.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_cover.jpg?resize=320%2C446&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_cover.jpg?resize=600%2C836&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_cover.jpg?resize=240%2C334&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_cover.jpg?resize=768%2C1069&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_cover.jpg?resize=1103%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 1103w\" /></a></p><p>Here we are, bewildered miracles of chemistry and chance, trembling embers of dead stars capable of sign and song, a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/04/30/bet/\">wild bet</a> against probability that won. </p>\n<p>We have dreamt up origin myths and cosmological models, built the Taj Mahal and the Large Hadron Collider, to fathom where we came from and where we are going. We have invented mathematics to describe the mystery we live in and poetry to describe the mystery we are. But beneath it all, we are born knowing — though we spend our lives unlearning — the elemental truth about us: A human being is a living question the only answer to which is love. </p>\n<p>That is what emanates from the pages of Azita Ardakani’s uncommonly wonderful <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>Ocean of Stars</em></strong></a> (<a href=\"https://search.worldcat.org/title/1573476604\" target=\"_blank\"><em>public library</em></a>). Like all great children’s books, it is a work of philosophy disguised as a painted poem — one Azita composed while trying to conceive her first child, reckoning with the alien wonder of how a small universe could grow inside the ocean of her body.</p>\n<p>Having grown up with a Sufi mother and made a home in the biological sciences, she weaves together scientific fact and poetic truth into a modern cosmogony that unfolds like a lullaby, a prayer for belonging, a blessing for life. </p>\n<p>The story came to her the way love does — unbidden, unreasoned, unasked for: a visitation of extraordinary clarity in a moment of pure presence with wild nature, arriving so fully formed that she had to run home from the forest to transcribe it. </p>\n<p>Artist <a href=\"https://www.rebeccarebouche.com\" target=\"_blank\">Rebecca Rebouché</a>, who had never worked on a children’s book before, created a breathtaking visual language to meet the story’s whimsy, painting on a single master canvas more than seven feet wide, then dividing it by the golden ratio into frames to make each spread of the book. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_canvas.jpg?resize=680%2C509&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"509\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_canvas.jpg?w=1048&amp;ssl=1 1048w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_canvas.jpg?resize=320%2C240&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_canvas.jpg?resize=600%2C449&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_canvas.jpg?resize=240%2C180&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars_canvas.jpg?resize=768%2C575&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars1.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars1.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars1.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars1.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars1.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars1.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>Once upon a time, in a far away place,<br />\ndarkness drifted, knowing no time.<br />\nReaching for infinity,<br />\nonly knowing beyond. </p>\n<p>One day, in the web of inky<br />\nendlessness, it asked itself:<br />\n“Can I see you?”</p>\n<p>The darkness<br />\nwaited and waited.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars2.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars2.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars2.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars2.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars2.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars2.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>And then, in answer,<br />\na star.<br />\nAnd then another<br />\nand another and another.<br />\nAnother is where<br />\nreflection began.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars3.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars3.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars3.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars3.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars3.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars3.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars4.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars4.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars4.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars4.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars4.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars4.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>As the cosmological story moves from stars to sentience — we see our Pale Blue Dot form “to reflect the stars back to themselves,” we see the “star beings” constellate out of the cosmic dust and descend “to touch the ocean, to greet themselves” — a sense of interbeing begins to emerge, a tender awareness that without this reflection, without this reciprocity between thing and thing, between one and all, nothing would exist. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars12.jpg?resize=680%2C479&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"479\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars12.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars12.jpg?resize=320%2C226&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars12.jpg?resize=600%2C423&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars12.jpg?resize=240%2C169&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars12.jpg?resize=768%2C541&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars5.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars5.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars5.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars5.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars5.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars5.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>The water stars<br />\nstretched onto the soil,<br />\nmixed into the clay,<br />\nand became…<br />\neverything.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars6.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars6.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars6.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars6.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars6.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars6.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars14.jpg?resize=680%2C506&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"506\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars14.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars14.jpg?resize=320%2C238&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars14.jpg?resize=600%2C447&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars14.jpg?resize=240%2C179&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars14.jpg?resize=768%2C572&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars7.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars7.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars7.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars7.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars7.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars7.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>Mixed from clay and star,<br />\nflesh and breath,<br />\na hollow canal opened<br />\nso life could reach back<br />\nto the darkness.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars8.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars8.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars8.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars8.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars8.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars8.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars13_1.jpg?resize=680%2C567&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"567\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars13_1.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars13_1.jpg?resize=320%2C267&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars13_1.jpg?resize=600%2C501&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars13_1.jpg?resize=240%2C200&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars13_1.jpg?resize=768%2C641&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Page by page comes the quickening that this is not a myth of creation but a truth of homecoming, not a new learning but an elemental remembering. The story ends with a spell against forgetting what we are:</p>\n<blockquote><p>Once upon a time, in a far away place,<br />\ndarkness drifted and you drifted inside of it.</p>\n<p>You are the wish<br />\nyou once wished for.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Ocean-Stars-Azita-Ardakani/dp/1592704913/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars20.jpg?resize=680%2C566&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"566\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars20.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars20.jpg?resize=320%2C266&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars20.jpg?resize=600%2C499&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars20.jpg?resize=240%2C200&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/oceanofstars20.jpg?resize=768%2C639&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Azita writes in the author’s afterword:</p>\n<blockquote><p>We live in a time of deep forgetting. </p>\n<p>The living world has become something we visit, something we manage, something outside ourselves. We move through days full of noise and urgency, rarely stopping to feel the improbable intimacy of being alive. In losing touch with our kinship to all that is, we have also lost something within ourselves — a felt sense of being part of a story far larger than the span of a single life. In its absence, many of us carry a quiet loneliness, untethered from wonder, from awe, from the deep reassurance of being held by something vast and alive.</p>\n<p>Perhaps this is why the stories that help us to remember matter so much. To remember is not to retrieve something lost. It is to come home, again and again, to the mystery that has been here all along, patiently waiting for us to notice and to shine once more.</p></blockquote>\n<p>What emerges from this scroll of wonder is a reminder that we are here to mirror and magnify the light between us and within us; that this rapturous reflection — which poet Diane Ackerman so unforgettably calls <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/02/24/diane-ackerman-the-planets/\">“the ricochet wonder of it all: the plain everythingness of everything, in cahoots with the everythingness of everything else”</a> — is our cosmic inheritance, is the redemption of our transience, is love. </p>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"4d01889e1f74fa67f301f6c18292669bc2a4dcff19577f256e41421c108ce14c","category":"Sites"}